This tree is a fork of Neroued/ninfer at commit feaf4dd. The modifications add
tensor-parallel execution across two GPUs and YaRN positional scaling for
1,048,576-token contexts to the 27B execution package. They touch, in summary:

  * src/core           two-device ExecutionContext; per-device arenas, streams
                       and graph objects; per-device memoization of kernel
                       attribute opt-ins
  * src/ops            allreduce_sum and allgather collectives; column- and
                       row-parallel split forms of the nine Op families that
                       carry sharded weights; a 12-Q-head/2-KV-head GQA
                       geometry; a YaRN frequency-buffer rope kernel; a
                       1,048,576-key visible-key domain and the shared-memory
                       accounting that goes with it
  * src/artifact       sharded weight and shard plans, and the materialization
                       that binds a shard of a tensor to one device
  * src/targets        two-rank Program wiring: split prefill, decode, MTP and
                       output-head schedules; cross-device graph capture and
                       replay; peer state publication
  * src/runtime,       --tp / --devices / --rope / --yarn-* plumbing through the
    src/serve, apps    public Engine, the CLI and the server
  * eval/, tools/tp2/  1M needle, soak and power runners; P2P, capture and
                       transport probes; the tp1-to-tp2 parity harness; the
                       vLLM YaRN reference dumper
  * tests/, scripts/   split-Op oracles, dual-device integration and graph
                       tests, the YaRN drift guard, and the tp1 golden-token
                       identity gate against upstream feaf4dd

Single-GPU (--tp 1) behaviour is unchanged from feaf4dd; see
tests/data/tp1-golden/MANIFEST.md for the token-level comparison.

